Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: concurrent candidate queries complete and time out on their own

0222 lets queries to different agents run at once. Two paths still assumed
one query of the type at a time, and in the room some radios' queries were
refused as not ready for minutes (candidate measurement never complete):

- A reply (metrics or an all-rejected Ack) completed the active query of the
  type found first, not the one of the radio that answered: the answering
  radio's command stayed active, another agent's was destroyed early.
- The generic timeout reads the type's time, the longest any query took
  since the type was last idle. With four agents queried continuously the
  type never went idle, so after 10 s every check cancelled every agent's
  query.

A reply completes the command of the radio that answered, and a candidate
query times out from its own start and cancels only itself.

Upstream-Status: Pending

